# Performance first

For this project (and sites built in this studio style), **performance is the top priority**.

- Target **maximum sustainable FPS** and buttery scroll/animation — prefer 60fps (or device refresh) under real mobile Safari/Chrome, not only desktop.
- When trade-offs appear (visual richness vs smoothness), **choose smoothness** unless the user explicitly accepts a cost.
- Avoid known compositor killers unless replaced with a cheaper equivalent:
  - SVG `feTurbulence` / heavy SVG filters on large surfaces (confirmed: alone can drop iOS ~60→24) — use tiling noise texture instead
  - Stacking live WebGL + heavy DOM morph + scrubbed filters in the same frame
- Prefer **baked / static assets** (tiling noise PNG/WebP, precomputed paths, instancing) over procedural per-frame work.
- **Grain/noise is a global concern**, not an iOS-only patch: fix the technique for all platforms (e.g. texture overlay), don’t leave `feTurbulence` as the canonical approach.
- Organic `clip-path: path(...)` is allowed when the grain path is cheap; don’t re-disable it as an iOS-only shortcut without measuring.
- Profile on real devices; desktop FPS is not proof. A/B expensive effects one at a time.
- Do not reintroduce disabled expensive effects “for beauty” without an explicit user request and a measured plan.
